<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!DOCTYPE plist PUBLIC "-//Apple//DTD PLIST 1.0//EN" "http://www.apple.com/DTDs/PropertyList-1.0.dtd">
<plist version="1.0">
<dict>
  <!--
    Entitlements for the app itself. Almost empty on purpose.

    NOT PRESENT, and must never be added:

      com.apple.security.app-sandbox

    App Sandbox breaks this app in two unrecoverable ways. A sandboxed process cannot
    spawn and supervise an arbitrary child (the Node sidecar) outside its container,
    and it cannot usefully call sandbox-exec, because Seatbelt profiles do not nest:
    the outer container already denies what the inner profile would have to grant.
    That is also why Mac App Store distribution is not available — App Review requires
    the sandbox, and guideline 2.5.2 separately prohibits executing downloaded code
    that changes app functionality, which is the whole product. Direct download with
    Developer ID, notarization and Sparkle is the distribution path.

    The app needs no JIT and loads no third-party libraries of its own, so it takes
    the strictest hardened-runtime posture available: nothing relaxed here. The
    sidecar's separate signature carries the relaxations V8 needs — see
    Sidecar.entitlements.
  -->
</dict>
</plist>
